# 21. AI-Assisted Writing Rules

When using AI to draft GPL content:

1. Assume the reader is technically informed.
2. Start at the useful insight.
3. Do not explain normal production conditions.
4. Do not expand every assignment bullet into prose.
5. Use connected reasoning.
6. Avoid statement stacking.
7. Avoid claim + list + consequence structure.
8. Use examples only when they clarify the mechanism.
9. Avoid lists disguised as prose.
10. Avoid unnecessary contrast framing.
11. Do not create staged insight lines.
12. Do not repeat obvious operational consequences.
13. Let the argument determine the structure.
14. Do not write to length.
15. Cut paragraphs that do not add new information or inference.
16. Keep GPL positioning restrained.
17. Do not use AEO terminology as filler.
18. Stop when the argument is complete.

